   "source": [
    "### 2.1 Remove malformed rows\n",
    "\n",
    "The label columns load as `object` instead of numbers, and there are more rows than the original\n",
    "Jigsaw file (~159.5k). Both are signs that some multi-line comments were split into **junk rows**\n",
    "during CSV parsing — text ends up in label columns. Previously these rows were filled with `0`\n",
    "and silently counted as *clean*, which pollutes the training data. We drop every row whose comment\n",
    "is missing or whose labels are not exactly 0 or 1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "f6f99e8e",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[LABEL_COLS] = df[LABEL_COLS].apply(pd.to_numeric, errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "valid = (\n",
    "    df['comment_text'].notna() &\n",
    "    df['comment_text'].astype(str).str.strip().ne('') &\n",
    "    df[LABEL_COLS].isin([0, 1]).all(axis=1)\n",
    ")\n",
    "n_before = len(df)\n",
    "df = df[valid].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "df[LABEL_COLS] = df[LABEL_COLS].astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Dropped {n_before - len(df):,} malformed rows')\n",
    "print(f'Clean dataset: {len(df):,} rows')"
   ]
  },
