  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3c9f8d34",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Data Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing pipeline consists of:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Step | Action | Rationale |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Sampling** | Take `SAMPLE_SIZE` random rows (or all) | Manageable compute cost |\n",
    "| **Length filter** | Keep comments ≤ 400 chars | Remove noise from very long posts |\n",
    "| **Lowercasing** | `str.lower()` | Normalise case |\n",
    "| **Punctuation removal** | `str.maketrans` | Remove non-alphabetic noise |\n",
    "| **Lemmatisation** | `WordNetLemmatizer` | Reduce words to base form |\n",
    "| **Stemming** | `PorterStemmer` | Further normalise tokens |\n",
    "| **Stop word removal** | NLTK English stopwords | Remove uninformative tokens |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "28efbfa5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 4.1  Sample & shuffle\n",
    "n_rows = len(df) if SAMPLE_SIZE is None else min(SAMPLE_SIZE, len(df))\n",
    "dataset_sub = df.sample(n_rows, random_state=RANDOM_STATE).reset_index(drop=True)  # sample() also shuffles\n",
    "print(f'Subset: {dataset_sub.shape[0]:,} rows')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "78de56b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 4.2  Length filter\n",
    "mask = (\n",
    "    dataset_sub['comment_text'].notna() &\n",
    "    dataset_sub['comment_text'].apply(lambda x: isinstance(x, str) and len(x) <= MAX_COMMENT_LEN)\n",
    ")\n",
    "dataset_filtered = dataset_sub[mask].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "comments = dataset_filtered['comment_text'].tolist()\n",
    "labels   = dataset_filtered[LABEL_COLS].to_numpy(dtype=int)\n",
    "\n",
    "retained_pct = len(comments) / len(dataset_sub) * 100\n",
    "print(f'After length filter: {len(comments):,} comments retained ({retained_pct:.1f}%)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "79ab4434",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 4.3  Text cleaning pipeline\n",
    "punctuation_chars = string.punctuation.replace(\"'\", '') + '0123456789'\n",
    "trantab    = str.maketrans(punctuation_chars, ' ' * len(punctuation_chars))\n",
    "stop_words = set(stopwords.words('english')) | {''} | {chr(c) for c in range(ord('b'), ord('z')+1)}\n",
    "\n",
    "lemmatiser = WordNetLemmatizer()\n",
    "stemmer    = PorterStemmer()\n",
    "\n",
    "def clean_text(text: str) -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Lowercase → strip punctuation/digits → lemmatise → stem → remove stopwords.\"\"\"\n",
    "    text   = text.lower().translate(trantab)\n",
    "    tokens = [\n",
    "        stemmer.stem(lemmatiser.lemmatize(w, pos='v'))\n",
    "        for w in text.split()\n",
    "        if w not in stop_words\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    return ' '.join(tokens)\n",
    "\n",
    "comments_clean = [clean_text(c) for c in comments]\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Sample — before:', comments[0][:120])\n",
    "print('Sample — after :', comments_clean[0][:120])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c0f47ab4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Train / Test Split & Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "We **split first** and fit every vectoriser on the training text only. Fitting on all comments\n",
    "lets vocabulary and IDF weights from the test set leak into training, which makes test scores\n",
    "look better than they really are.\n",
    "\n",
    "The split is **stratified** on \"any toxic label\", so train and test have the same share of toxic comments.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two vectorisation strategies are built:\n",
    "- **Bag-of-Words (BoW)** — raw term counts\n",
    "- **TF-IDF** — term frequency weighted by inverse document frequency (down-weights very common terms)\n",
    "\n",
    "Matrices are kept **sparse** (no `.toarray()`), which uses far less memory and lets us train on more data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e5f53517",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 5.1  Stratified train / test split on the cleaned text\n",
    "any_toxic = (labels.sum(axis=1) > 0).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "comments_train, comments_test, Y_train, Y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    comments_clean, labels,\n",
    "    test_size=TEST_SIZE,\n",
    "    stratify=any_toxic,\n",
    "    random_state=RANDOM_STATE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "STOP_LIST = list(stop_words)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Vectoriser 1: Bag-of-Words\n",
    "bow_vectoriser = CountVectorizer(stop_words=STOP_LIST, max_features=10_000)\n",
    "X_bow_train = bow_vectoriser.fit_transform(comments_train)\n",
    "X_bow_test  = bow_vectoriser.transform(comments_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Vectoriser 2: TF-IDF (unigrams)\n",
    "tfidf_vectoriser = TfidfVectorizer(stop_words=STOP_LIST, max_features=10_000, sublinear_tf=True)\n",
    "X_tfidf_train = tfidf_vectoriser.fit_transform(comments_train)\n",
    "X_tfidf_test  = tfidf_vectoriser.transform(comments_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Vectoriser 3: TF-IDF with bigrams (1–2 grams)\n",
    "# Bigrams capture multi-word toxic phrases such as 'go die', 'you idiot',\n",
    "# which unigram models miss entirely.\n",
    "ngram_vectoriser = TfidfVectorizer(\n",
    "    stop_words=STOP_LIST,\n",
    "    ngram_range=(1, 2),      # unigrams AND bigrams\n",
    "    max_features=20_000,     # larger vocab to accommodate bigrams\n",
    "    sublinear_tf=True,\n",
    "    min_df=2                 # ignore terms appearing in fewer than 2 documents\n",
    ")\n",
    "X_ngram_train = ngram_vectoriser.fit_transform(comments_train)\n",
    "X_ngram_test  = ngram_vectoriser.transform(comments_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Train / test     : {len(comments_train):,} / {len(comments_test):,}')\n",
    "print(f'BoW         train: {X_bow_train.shape[0]:,} × {X_bow_train.shape[1]:,}')\n",
    "print(f'TF-IDF      train: {X_tfidf_train.shape[0]:,} × {X_tfidf_train.shape[1]:,}')\n",
    "print(f'TF-IDF ngram train: {X_ngram_train.shape[0]:,} × {X_ngram_train.shape[1]:,}')\n",
    "print(f'\\nBigrams expand the feature space by '\n",
    "      f'{X_ngram_train.shape[1] - X_tfidf_train.shape[1]:,} additional features.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "998df831",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Top tokens by total frequency\n",
    "token_freqs = pd.Series(np.asarray(X_bow_train.sum(axis=0)).ravel(),\n",
    "                        index=bow_vectoriser.get_feature_names_out())\n",
    "top_tokens  = token_freqs.nlargest(20)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "top_tokens[::-1].plot(kind='barh', color=sns.color_palette('Blues_r', 20), ax=ax, edgecolor='white')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Figure 4 — Top 20 Most Frequent Tokens (after preprocessing)', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Total Count in Corpus')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0dc13326",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Class Balance After the Split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "37c5e66b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f'Training samples : {X_bow_train.shape[0]:,}')\n",
    "print(f'Test samples     : {X_bow_test.shape[0]:,}')\n",
    "print(f'Label matrix     : {Y_train.shape[1]} classes')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Class imbalance summary\n",
    "print('\\n Positive rate per label (train vs test)')\n",
    "for ix, lbl in enumerate(LABEL_DISPLAY):\n",
    "    pos = Y_train[:, ix].sum()\n",
    "    pct = pos / len(Y_train) * 100\n",
    "    pct_test = Y_test[:, ix].mean() * 100\n",
    "    bar = '█' * int(pct * 2)\n",
    "    print(f'  {lbl:15s}: {pos:5d} ({pct:5.1f}%) | test {pct_test:5.1f}%  {bar}')"
   ]
