   "id": "9aa9fac1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Model 1 — Baseline\n",
    "### Binary Relevance + Multinomial Naïve Bayes (BoW)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why start here?**  \n",
    "Multinomial NB is the canonical text classification baseline: fast, interpretable, and well-suited to sparse BoW counts. Its results give us a performance floor that every subsequent model must beat.\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⚠ **Class imbalance note:** NB has no built-in mechanism for imbalanced classes. It will be biased toward predicting the majority (clean) class — this is the key weakness we address in Model 2."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5530b931",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train\n",
    "nb_classifiers = train_binary_relevance(MultinomialNB, X_bow_train, Y_train, alpha=1.0)\n",
    "Y_pred_nb      = predict_binary_relevance(nb_classifiers, X_bow_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "metrics_nb = evaluate_multilabel(Y_test, Y_pred_nb, 'BR — Multinomial Naïve Bayes (BoW)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b76a17b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Per-label classification report\n",
    "print('Per-label Classification Report — Naïve Bayes\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "for ix, label in enumerate(LABEL_DISPLAY):\n",
    "    print(f'▸ {label}')\n",
    "    print(classification_report(\n",
    "        Y_test[:, ix],\n",
    "        Y_pred_nb[:, ix],\n",
    "        target_names=['Not Toxic', 'Toxic'],\n",
    "        zero_division=0\n",
