    "---\n",
    "## 13. Conclusions & Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "The numeric findings are printed by the cell above, so they always match the current run.\n",
    "General observations:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Finding | Detail |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **Class imbalance is the core challenge** | ~90% of comments are clean, which biases models toward predicting 0 |\n",
    "| **Class weighting helps** | `class_weight='balanced'` lifts recall on rare labels compared to plain Naïve Bayes |\n",
    "| **SMOTE is not a clear win on text** | Interpolating sparse TF-IDF vectors creates unrealistic samples; check the table above before relying on it |\n",
    "| **Chains vs. Binary Relevance is close** | Label dependencies exist, but a well-tuned independent SVM can match or beat the chain |\n",
    "| **Rare labels remain hard** | `threat` and `identity_hate` have very few positives, so their F1 is the lowest and the least stable |\n",
    "\n",
    "###  Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "| Priority | Improvement | Expected Impact |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| High | **Use the full dataset** (`SAMPLE_SIZE = None`) | More examples of rare labels |\n",
    "| High | **BERT / RoBERTa fine-tuning** | Contextual embeddings — largest potential gain |\n",
    "| Medium | **Calibrated probabilities** (`CalibratedClassifierCV`) | Meaningful confidence scores in the app |\n",
    "| Medium | **Per-label decision thresholds** | Trade precision vs. recall per label |\n",
    "| Low | **Error analysis on FP/FN** | Understand remaining failure modes |\n",
    "\n",
